From: Salty <99386653+PjSalty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:22:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] migrations: restore inherited rating scores in
 MigrateRatingLevels

Intent: MigrateRatingLevels rewrites the stored score of every item from
its own OfficialRating, which sets InheritedParentalRatingValue and
InheritedParentalRatingSubValue to NULL on every item that has no rating
of its own. Before the routine ran, those rows carried the score of
their show: OnMetadataChanged derives it from the display parent on
every save. List queries filter on the stored column and treat NULL as
unrated, so from the routine until the next save of each item a profile
with a rating limit that does not block unrated items is listed the
seasons and episodes of shows above its limit (detail and playback
still refuse them, those check the rating in memory). Upstream re-dated
the routine at 12.1 and again at 12.2, so every existing database went
through that on both upgrades: 6,985 rows on the library this was found
on, put right only by the first full library scan. After the per-rating
loop, give each unscored item without a rating of its own the stored
score of its display parent (episode -> season -> series, anything else
-> parent), one level per pass until a pass changes nothing, inside the
routine's transaction. Items with a custom rating are left to the next
save, as the routine leaves them today. Includes a test.
Ceiling: builds on the test file 0020 adds and shares its ceiling: the
routine's file name carries its date, so the patch is rebased onto each
re-dated file. The walk reads the stored SeasonId, SeriesId and
ParentId; an item type that starts overriding DisplayParentId needs a
branch here.
Drop when: upstream scores inherited ratings in the routine, or stops
filtering lists on the stored column.

Patch: 0027
